; A module exporting a macro whose template names a function it
; keeps private, for the MAC-HYG-11 case. `helper` resolves at the
; macro's own definition site - the same module - so the definition
; is clean; the refusal comes at an outside invocation, where the
; expanded name does not exist.
(pub macro (once x) (helper x))

(:: helper (-> Int Int))
(fn (helper n)
  (* n 2))
